				""
				"&a&lSuper disk array: &r&ais referred to as SDA. When storing disks (infinite disks), it is called &n\"disk array\" or \"DASDA\" &r&a; when storing items, it is called &n\"storage array\" or \"SASDA\" &r&aUsed to package large storage needs, such as \"Programming Circuit Disk Array\", which represents internal storage of unlimited storage disks related to programming circuits"
				""
				"&l&aAfter version 2.7.5, SDA has built-in NBT optimization, using three layers of optimization: 1. Internal NBT simplification, 2. Serialized KEY hash optimization, 3. NBT is changed to external storage and is not stored in the SDA item body NBT, using UUID identification."
				"&l&cNote: You must install the SDA UUID identification file under /kubejs/data/sda_uuid_store/, otherwise the task SDA collection is directly a rolling log"
