		{
			can_repeat: true
			dependencies: ["72553FB6258F5893"]
			description: [
				"&l&aInstructions for use:"
				"&aThe Singularity hub disk warehouse is mounted at a fixed location in the structure and is managed and scheduled by the host. The disk warehouse can accommodate up to 256 (configurable) disks. The default is 108 slots. Only unlimited disks are recommended, and only unlimited disks can use such a large slot."
				""
				"If &eis placed in a \"disk array\" and there is an infinite disk/arbitrary storage disk inside the array, the storage details of the internal disk will be exposed to AE."
				"&eFor example: after the unlimited water disk is placed in the \"Disk Array\" and \"ME Disk Warehouse\", the connected AE network will accept the unlimited water disk information and allow disk calls."
				""
				"&cThere is currently a bug: no host is required, the warehouse can be used independently and connected to the Internet. I don’t really want to fix it."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_1.png width:100 height:160 align:left fit:true}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_2.png width:100 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_3.png width:150 height:100 align:center fit:true}(new page placeholder text)"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&cThat day, dishanhai created 6,000 unlimited disks, and then found out in despair that the drive only had 20 slots, so he forced dishanhai to stuff 300 drives, and then dishanhai created this multi-block machine... This is a sad story"
				"&e- I hope no one has to worry about stuffing a bunch of disks in with a bunch of drives anymore"
			]
			icon: "gt_shanhai:singularity_data_hub"
			id: "34ADD9CF16297495"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "24F2D58DF45834E4"
					item: {
