		{
			can_repeat: true
			dependencies: ["2625AFA18C6B7B82"]
			description: [
				"&e&l1. &aYou must first place the submitter and right-click the submitter to open its UI to claim the submitter, and then connect it to the AE network (cable connection, etc.)"
				""
				"&e&l2. &aAfter you complete item 1, you can press the green plus sign above \"Target\" to mount the specified task to the specified submitter queue"
				""
				"&e&l3. &aAfter you complete item 2, make sure there are corresponding items in the AE network you are connected to, otherwise the submission will be invalid. The task rewards after submission will be automatically received in the connected AE network storage"
				""
				"&e&lFunction analysis: &71. \"Complete Prompt\" whether to block the prompt after the task is completed. It is not blocked by default. If it is turned on, it will only block the tasks mounted by the submitter;"
				"&l&72. \"Reward Collection\" by default only automatically collects rewards from mounted tasks into AE. After switching, it becomes a global task behavior and will collect rewards from other tasks into AE and is not limited to mounted tasks."
				""
				"&e&lAdditional tips: &7It is extremely suitable for repeated submission tasks, such as lottery draws, submitting a large number of items, etc. I may make a separate module because I have not seen the same type of attachment, so I made FTBQ performance optimization"
				""
				"&7View picture analysis on the next page"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_6.png width:100 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_7.png width:100 height:70 align:center fit:true}"
			]
			icon: "gt_shanhai:ftbq_ae_submitter"
			id: "7C8CD0964CC12F68"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "0CEC0D28A2164916"
					item: "gt_shanhai:ftbq_ae_submitter"
					random_bonus: 3
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "You probably saw the green plus sign in the upper corner of the task \"Target\". It is for the automatic submitter."
